From ad5f0b2af1e6f5db86e2f88732be8582f081336b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:06:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] i18n(ru): translate remaining bare literals; point source
 links at the fork

A sweep rather than another one-at-a-time fix. Bare literals never reach
the catalog, so lingui cannot translate them in any locale, and they are
invisible to a coverage count -- the modal that prompted this had a
translated body under an English title and English buttons.

Found by scanning for JSX text nodes and string-valued title/text props
that are not wrapped in <Trans>: the two create/join dialogs, the desktop
titlebar's connection states, role hoisting, the appearance colour heading
and font preview, account deletion results, the add-bot warnings, and the
search and pinned message sidebar titles. Sixteen new catalog entries.

Two incidental fixes. "Bots are not verified by Stoat" was leftover
branding and now refers to the instance. The font preview pangram is
translated to a Russian one, which is the point of a pangram -- the Latin
sentence exercises none of the glyphs a Cyrillic user is previewing.

Source Code links in settings and on the auth page pointed at upstream;
they now point at this fork, as AGPL-3.0 section 13 requires of a modified
network service.
